course: dictionary
lesson: 807
title: Beginners
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A beginner is a person who is just starting to learn or do something, and does not have much skill yet. Everyone is a beginner at first, so you do not need to feel embarrassed about it. «Guitar strings hurt beginners' fingertips» tells you that beginners are people who have only just started playing.
explain: Use the words around beginner to work out its meaning. On a sign, «for beginners» means the class is for people who are new. In «a complete beginner», the word complete shows that the person knows nothing yet. Clues like these help you understand a word without a dictionary.
explain: Notice the form beginners' in «beginners' fingertips». The apostrophe comes after the s because the fingertips belong to many beginners. Knowing this helps you read the sentence correctly.
fact: A beginner is someone who is just starting and does not have much skill yet.
fact: «For beginners» on a sign means the class or activity is made for people who are new.
fact: «A complete beginner» means someone who is totally new and knows nothing yet.
fact: After «a few weeks of short regular practice», a beginner's fingers form calluses, which are patches of hardened skin, and the pain fades.
exercise: «Priya's team were beginners, happily losing to other beginners.» What is a beginner? | *A person who is just starting and does not have much skill yet | A person who has won every game for years | A referee who decides the score | A person who is always late
exercise: In swimming, skiing or skating, where should beginners stay? | In the deepest part of the pool | *In safe areas with an instructor | Wherever they like | Alone, far away from everyone
exercise: «A complete beginner» means someone who is what? | Very famous | Tired after a long day | *Totally new, knowing nothing yet | The best in the class
test: What does the sign «for beginners» tell you about a class? | It is free to join at any time of day | It is cancelled today | *It is made for people who are new to the activity | It is only for experts
test: Why do «beginners' fingertips» hurt when they first play guitar, and what happens after a few weeks? | Fingers only hurt when it is cold | *The strings press on the skin, and practice makes calluses that toughen and stop the pain | Guitars are too heavy to hold | Guitar strings are sharp, and the pain gets worse each week
exam: Which sentence uses beginner correctly to mean someone who has just started? | A beginner is a type of fruit found in shops. | The beginner won the world championship ten years in a row. | *Everyone is a beginner at first, so it is okay to make mistakes. | Beginners are not allowed in the pool, since they are experts.
